# Colour design system (ENG-DESIGN-COLOR-001)

The full specification is `docs/standards/COLOR-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md`. Read it
before you:

- create a new component or page
- change any colour, state, theme or palette
- refactor or visually redesign UI

The essentials, which the specification and its tests enforce:

- Components use token utilities only (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`,
  `bg-sidebar`, …). Do not use Tailwind palette colours (`bg-blue-600`,
  `text-white`), arbitrary colours (`bg-[#…]`), inline style colours or
  `--palette-*` in components.
- A palette change is `resources/design-system/palette.json` plus
  `npm run palette`. Never edit the generated `palette.css` or `themes.css`,
  and never recolour components to change the palette.
- A missing colour role means adding a token (specification §11), not adding a
  literal.
- Every new text/background pairing is a declared, contrast-tested pair, in
  every theme (WCAG 2.2 AA). Colour is never the only signal.
- Exceptions only via `resources/design-system/exceptions.json`, with owner
  approval.
